Package: lennys-benchmark
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libstdc++6 (>= 12), libgcc-s1 (>= 3.0), libepoxy0, libx11-6, libgl1
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: @HOMEPAGE@
Description: CPU + GPU benchmark with OpenGL rendering
 lennys-benchmark is a self-contained CPU and GPU benchmark for Linux.
 .
 The CPU suite runs multi-threaded integer, FP32, FP64 and memory-bandwidth
 tests with a scaling analysis.  The GPU suite opens an X11 window and renders
 a demanding OpenGL 4.5 scene (procedural torus-knot model, instancing,
 physically based shading, six dynamic lights, HDR, bloom, ACES tonemapping)
 and measures geometry and fill throughput.
 .
 The program detects the CPU, all integrated and discrete GPUs and reports
 temperatures, clocks and power draw.  On hybrid systems with an NVIDIA GPU it
 automatically uses PRIME render offload.
